@startuml
allowmixing
title cd - Statistics data type and C++ artifacts
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
package "cpp_learning::statistics" {
  class Statistics <<struct>> {
    +count : std::size_t
    +minimum : double
    +maximum : double
    +mean : double
  }
  artifact "statistics.hpp" as Core
  artifact "cli.hpp / cli.cpp" as CLI
  Core ..> Statistics : declares / returns
  CLI ..> Core : implementation uses
  note left of Core
    Free function (not a class method):
    Statistics compute_statistics(
      const std::vector<double>& values)
    Throws invalid_argument or overflow_error.
    Input is borrowed and never retained.
  end note
  note right of CLI
    Free functions (not class methods):
    std::vector<double> parse_values(std::istream& input)
    int run(std::istream& input,
      std::ostream& output, std::ostream& error)
    Parsing returns an owning vector by value.
    run translates specified failures to exit status 1.
  end note
  note bottom of Statistics
    Value semantics; default special members.
    Successful result: count > 0, finite fields,
    extrema selected from input, mean = sum/count.
  end note
}
@enduml
